-- title:
--   Local images under the idelic Artin map: decomposition and inertia
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ and $F$ be number fields with $F/E$ Galois, the group $G=\mathrm{Gal}(F/E)$ being cyclic (and carrying the commutativity instance). Let $\mathfrak f$ be an ideal of $\mathcal O_E$ which is an admissible modulus of degree $[F:E]$, i.e. $\mathfrak f \neq \bot$ and for every finite place $v$ of $E$ at which the inertia subgroup of the chosen prime `primeAbove E F v` in $G$ is nontrivial, $v^{\,\mathrm{admissibleExpOfDegree}\,E\,[F:E]\,v}$ divides $\mathfrak f$. Let $r \colon (\mathbb A_E)^\times \to G$ be a group homomorphism such that: the principal ideles, i.e. the image of $E^\times$, lie in $\ker r$; $\ker r$ is exactly the subgroup generated by the principal ideles together with the image of the idelic norm attached to `genuineBaseChange E F` (the map on unit groups induced by the adelic norm $(\mathbb A_F)^\times \to (\mathbb A_E)^\times$); $r$ is surjective; and for every idele unit $u$ satisfying `IsAdjuster E 𝔣 u 1` (at each finite place $v$ dividing $\mathfrak f$ the finite component of $u$ at $v$ has valuation $1$ and its distance to $1$ is at most $\exp(-\mathrm{ord}_v \mathfrak f)$, and $u$ has positive real coordinate at each real embedding of $E$), one has $r(u) = \prod^{\mathrm f}_{v} \mathrm{Frob}_v^{\,\mathrm{ord}_v(u)}$, the finprod over finite places of the Frobenius `artinFrob E F v` raised to the exponent `placeOrd` of the finite part of $u$ at $v$. Finally let $v$ be a finite place of $E$ and $w$ a finite place of $F$ lying under which $v$ sits, i.e. $w.\mathrm{under}(\mathcal O_E) = v$. The conclusion is twofold: first, the image under $r$ of the subgroup of idele units with trivial infinite part and finite component $1$ at every finite place other than $v$ equals the decomposition subgroup [`NumberField.PlaceDecomp.decomp E F w`](def/NumberField_PlaceDecompositionAction.html#L82), the decomposition subgroup in $G$ of the valuation subring of the $w$-valuation of $F$; second, the image under $r$ of the subgroup of those ideles which in addition are units at $v$ (component at $v$ and its inverse both integral in the $v$-adic completion) equals the inertia subgroup of $w$ in $G$.
--
--   This identifies the local components of the global Artin map at an arbitrary finite place, ramified places included: the local unit group at $v$ maps onto the inertia group of $w\mid v$ and the full local multiplicative group onto the decomposition group. It is used for the corresponding inclusion of the inertia group in the image of the unit ideles away from $v$, and thence in the local–global compatibility of the reciprocity map in the cyclic layer.
